From 3bcd72e67501c2e845def7d38bd6bd808419beb2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stefan Hertenberger <erde74@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 19:01:03 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 42/45] postscript: the functions declared (atof, malloc,
 error's arguments were wrong on a 64-bit machine)

The programs on APE (compiled -B) called the C library's and common's
functions undeclared, as returning int: postreverse's atof gave the
file's %%Version as garbage, download's malloc and realloc lost the high
half of their pointers on amd64, and misc.c's error took its arguments as
unsigned int while the callers passed strings for its %s (cut to 32 bits
on amd64). common/ext.h now includes stdlib.h, string.h and unistd.h for
the programs on APE and declares common's functions; error is variadic
(vfprintf), lineno and position printed with %ld; each program declares
its own functions before their use; tcpostio is compiled with
_POSIX_SOURCE (it uses read, fork, select) and waits for its child's
status in an int (an unsigned long got 4 of its 8 bytes on amd64);
its getline is fdgetline (POSIX 2008 has a getline with other
arguments).
tr2post, a native program, is not changed (libc.h declares it all).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
